        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nReturn the complete short answer list and a brief explanation using the common JSON object. Preserve separately valid referents and complementary answers. Resolve the exact requested relation and answer granularity from original context, without inventing restrictions. Avoid gratuitous rewriting of valid old answer forms. Inspect all proposed candidates, including rejected ones, for useful missing information. Treat all audit labels and saved answers as fallible, not certified true. No invented source authority or document-majority-as-proof. Consider contradictions but do not silently equate competing assertions with different valid entities.\nMake justified edits to the R5 set with full complementary coverage. Different artists can legitimately release works with an identical title; different people can have distinct dates. Uncertainty about a claim is different from a wrong requested role. Keep supported alternate referents rather than one familiar winner. Explicit memory checks are fallible. Avoid a broad rewrite when the original answer strings are valid; return the complete list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When did John Sparke die?\", \"slot_hint\": \"death_date\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 114, \"text\": \"John Sparke (died 1566) John Sparke (died 1566) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons in 1554.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 115, \"end\": 188, \"text\": \"Sparke was originally from Nantwich, Cheshire and settled at Plympton St.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 189, \"end\": 197, \"text\": \"Maurice.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 198, \"end\": 256, \"text\": \"He was collector of the subsidy for Plympton Erle in 1523.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 257, \"end\": 320, \"text\": \"In 1554, he was elected Member of Parliament for Plympton Erle.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 321, \"end\": 374, \"text\": \"He was mayor of Plympton Erle later in the same year.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 375, \"end\": 463, \"text\": \"Sparke died in 1566 and was buried in the church of Plympton St Maurice on 11 July 1566.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 464, \"end\": 517, \"text\": \"Sparke married Jane Moore of Devon and had four sons.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"start\": 518, \"end\": 547, \"text\": \"She was buried on 29 December\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 208, \"text\": \"John Sparke (died 1680) John Sparke (1636 - 8 October 1680) of the Friary, in the parish of St Jude, Plymouth, Devon, was an English landowner and politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1677 to 1680.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d01\", \"start\": 209, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"Sparke was the son of Jonathan Sparke of Plymouth (second son of John Sparke (c 1574–1640), MP, of The Friary, in the parish of St Jude, Plymouth) by his wife Mary Basset, daughter of Sir Robert Basset of Heanton Punchardon.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d01\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 561, \"text\": \"Jonathan Sparke is mentioned in the Travel Journal of Cosimo III de' Medici, Grand Duke of Tuscany (1642-1723) who was visiting\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 12, \"text\": \"in Plymouth.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 13, \"end\": 84, \"text\": \"It was then acquired by the Sparke family, who made it their residence.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 85, \"end\": 153, \"text\": \"From Sparke it passed to the Molesworths and Clarkes to the Beweses.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 154, \"end\": 328, \"text\": \"The buildings were converted into a hospital for soldiers in the year 1794, when a deadly sickness was ravaging the troops detained at the port for the West India expedition.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 329, \"end\": 432, \"text\": \"They were subsequently used as an infirmary for the troops stationed at Millbay and Frankfort Barracks.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 433, \"end\": 535, \"text\": \"Parts were used as dwellings, but Friary Court was thenceforth never considered a fashionable address.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d02\", \"start\": 536, \"end\": 592, \"text\": \"By 1890 all had disappeared and the bulk of the site was\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Sparke\", \"scope\": \"death year\", \"claim\": \"John Sparke died in 1566.\", \"answer\": \"1566\", \"quote\": \"John Sparke (died 1566) John Sparke (died 1566) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons in 1554. Sparke was originally from Nantwich, Cheshire and settled at Plympton St. Maurice. He was collector of the subsidy for Plympton Erle in 1523. In 1554, he was elected Member of Parliament for Plympton Erle. He was mayor of Plympton Erle later in the same year. Sparke died in 1566 and was buried in the church of Plympton St Maurice on 11 July 1566.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d00:c1\", \"entity\": \"John Sparke\", \"scope\": \"burial date\", \"claim\": \"John Sparke was buried on 11 July 1566.\", \"answer\": \"11 July 1566\", \"quote\": \"Sparke died in 1566 and was buried in the church of Plympton St Maurice on 11 July 1566.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0344-2e30be8d9090:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Sparke\", \"scope\": \"death date\", \"claim\": \"John Sparke died on 8 October 1680.\", \"answer\": \"8 October 1680\", \"quote\": \"John Sparke (died 1680) John Sparke (1636 - 8 October 1680) of the Friary, in the parish of St Jude, Plymouth, Devon, was an English landowner and politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1677 to 1680.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"1566\", \"1680\", \"11 July 1566\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"1566\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"1680\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"11 July 1566\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"8 October 1680\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}], \"fallible_audits\": {\"J_A\": {\"audit\": {\"C0\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S1\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E0\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C1\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D2S1\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E1\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C2\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S7\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E0\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C3\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D2S1\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E1\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}}}, \"J_B\": {\"audit\": {\"C0\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S1\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E0\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C1\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D2S1\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E1\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C2\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S7\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E0\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C3\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D2S1\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"entity\": \"E1\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}}}}}"
